        {
          "dimension": "Liquidity / cascade contagion",
          "level": "High",
          "note": "Single-day liquidation events routinely exceed $1B across perp and lending markets, and cascading forced sells — where liquidations push prices lower, triggering further liquidations — can compress weeks of losses into 15 minutes, as seen with the $1.4B BTC wipeout.",
          "source": "https://chain.link/article/liquidation-cascade-crypto-lending"
        },
        {
          "dimension": "Market / volatility",
          "level": "High",
          "note": "Correlated macro shocks such as the August 2024 Black Monday session drove BTC down 15% and eliminated $900M in crypto positions within 24 hours, demonstrating that liquidation cascades are not DeFi-isolated events but can be triggered by global equity sell-offs.",
          "source": "https://coinmarketcap.com/charts/liquidations/"
        },
        {
          "dimension": "Centralization",
          "level": "Medium",
          "note": "Protocols with admin keys capable of adjusting collateral ratios, liquidation thresholds, or oracle sources mid-session expose users to governance-by-surprise; decentralized alternatives require on-chain votes but introduce slower response to genuine risk.",
          "source": "https://eco.com/support/en/articles/14800882-best-defi-lending-protocols-2026-tvl-rates-risk"
        },
        {
          "dimension": "Counterparty / venue risk",
          "level": "Medium",
          "note": "Centralized exchange liquidation engines (Binance seeing an $8.21M single BTCUSDT liquidation, HTX handling a $98.46M BTC position) operate with proprietary mark-price mechanisms that can diverge from spot, forcing liquidations before on-chain prices would trigger them.",
          "source": "https://www.binance.com/en/support/faq/detail/360033525271"
        },
        {
          "dimension": "Oracle / price-feed manipulation",
